course: dictionary
lesson: 14631
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so the words around them show you which meaning the writer wants. The word potted is a good example. «She kept a potted plant on the windowsill.» The clues are plant and windowsill, so potted means growing in a pot.
explain: Now read «The Rat packed potted meat for the picnic.» The clues are meat, picnic and sandwiches. Potted meat is cooked meat pressed into a small jar and covered with fat or butter so it keeps. It is food, not a plant.
explain: Potted can also mean short and simple. «The teacher gave us a potted history of the castle in three lines.» Three lines is the clue: the long story was made short. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Potted describes something, like «a potted plant» or «potted meat».
fact: «Potted» can mean growing in a pot, like a flower in a flowerpot.
fact: «Potted meat» is cooked meat pressed into a small pot or jar and covered with fat or butter.
fact: «A potted history» is a short, simple account of a long story.
fact: «Potted» is also the past form of «pot», as in «she potted the ball» in snooker or pool.
exercise: «The potted plant sat by the front door.» What does potted mean here? | Cooked and covered with butter | Written in a few lines | *Growing in a pot | Lost in the garden
exercise: The Rat packed «potted meat» for the picnic. What is potted meat? | A plant that grows in the garden | *Cooked meat pressed into a jar and covered with fat | A long story about a farm | Meat that is still raw and red
exercise: «Mum gave us a potted history of the Romans in five minutes.» What does potted suggest here? | *Short and simple | Very long and detailed | Growing in a pot | Pressed into a jar
test: «He potted the red ball in the pocket.» What does potted mean here? | Written in a few lines | Cooked and pressed into a jar | *Knocked into a pocket | Put into a flowerpot
test: Which sentence uses potted as the past form of pot? | The potted plant is green | A potted history is short | Potted meat is good for picnics | *Yesterday I potted the seedling into a bigger pot
exam: Which meaning of potted fits «a potted history of the Tudors»? | *Short and simple | Growing in a pot | Pressed into a jar | Lost at sea
